# OS metadata
.DS_Store

# Editor metadata
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Python (the tool and its fixture generator are standard-library Python)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# The fixture media is *generated* test patterns, not source: 8 MB of DV and
# MPEG-1 stand-ins whose only job is to exercise the playback and copy-path
# paths. Run `python3 fixtures/make_fixtures.py` to rebuild it locally. The
# fixture *index* — and its stills — are committed, so the browser works from a
# fresh clone without ffmpeg or ImageMagick installed.
fixtures/media/

# An index is written beside the library it describes, so `fisean scan` run on
# this repository would drop one at the root. Only the root: the committed
# fixture lives in fixtures/fisean-index and must stay tracked.
/fisean-index/

# The indexer needs nothing else ignored: ffmpeg is run as a program and has no
# build output, and the models `fisean label` uses are cached by open_clip
# outside the repository, in ~/.cache/clip. **Correction (2026-10-01):** this
# note used to say the weights would earn a pattern here "when they are"
# downloaded. They are downloaded, and they earn nothing — nothing fetched for
# labelling lands in the tree, so there is no pattern to add. See AGENTS.md,
# "Keeping .gitignore current".
